        },
        "checks": checks,
        "theorem": {
            "name": "PolarizedPrimalOnlyRankOneTransportTheorem",
            "tier": "CLOSED_EXACT_EXECUTION_REDUCTION",
            "statement": "In a polarized B89 Gauss-Manin frame, horizontal transport preserves the nondegenerate self-pairing of every A1 vanishing vector. Its normalized polarization dual ell=e^TQ/(e^TQe) automatically obeys the adjoint horizontal equation and reconstructs the Picard-Lefschetz projector. Therefore the three selected common-frame projectors require three primal rank-1509 transports plus three certified common-base polarization applications, not three primal and three dual transports.",
        },
